---
id: air-fried-chicken-breast
title: Air-Fried Seasoned Chicken Breast
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 330

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Trim any excess fat or tenderloin tendon from @boneless-chicken-breast{1%package}. Pat thoroughly dry on all sides using paper towels to remove surface purge so the seasoning adheres evenly.

Rub the @boneless-chicken-breast evenly with @olive-oil{1%tsp}, then coat all sides with @kosher-salt{0.5%tsp}, @black-pepper{0.25%tsp}, @garlic-powder{0.5%tsp}, and @smoked-paprika{0.5%tsp}.

Preheat #air-fryer to 195°C (380°F). Place breasts in the basket in a single layer with space between them to allow 360-degree air circulation. Cook for ~air-fry-time{16%min}, flipping at the 9-minute mark, until the internal temperature reaches 71°C to 74°C (160°F–165°F) at the thickest part checked with a #meat-thermometer.

Let the chicken rest undisturbed for ~rest-time{5%min} so carryover heat completes cooking and juices redistribute into the meat fibers. Distribute whole breasts (or slice into thick medallions, ~165 g each) into 2 separate meal prep containers, drizzling any rested juices from the board over the portions.
